{
  "layout": "ozt_trade_tile",
  "note": "One tile of the trade screen: a thing's picture on its square, the price in gold at the bottom left, a count (bottom right on a wide tile, top right on a narrow one), a pip for its condition at the top right, and a coloured corner when it cannot be sold as it is. The root takes the pointer: a click and a drag land on it, and everything inside ignores the pointer, the picture too (a press on a picture that took the pointer never became a drag). The menu sizes the root to the tile's cells, then TileBg one pixel inside it, so that TileEdge shows as a border; the marks hang on the corners and follow (OZT_TradeTile.c). The marks stand at priority 610: the game draws an item's picture over its low siblings whatever their order (the vanilla icon keeps its picture at 151 and its count at 606).",
